(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-plate-preparation-decision :authorize-plate-processing-operation :proceed-with-plate-preparation-procedure :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007311-cloud-itonami-isco-7311-precision-instrument-makers-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the plate-preparation operation" "proceed with the plate preparation operation" "proceed with the plate-preparation procedure" "proceed with the plate processing procedure" "finalize the plate-preparation decision" "finalize the plate processing decision" "authorize the plate-preparation operation" "authorize the plate processing operation" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment" "override safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007321), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/pre-press-workshop-scheduling-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :worker-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7321"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007321: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7321 Pre-press Technicians workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7321\n-- Pre-press Technicians** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the\nrollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7321\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7321\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Pre-press Technicians\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7321` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7321` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nPre-press Technicians prepare print layouts and operate imaging/\nplate-making equipment involving chemical processing -- real\nphysical-safety stakes (chemical exposure from plate-processing\nsolutions, imaging/platemaking equipment hazards). The controlling\nconstraint for this vertical is that the closed op allowlist must\nNEVER include any op that directly finalizes a plate-preparation-\nexecution decision, or overrides a shop safety officer's judgment --\nthose decisions must always be a hard permanent block or an\nalways-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor is\ndeliberately scoped to SHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY --\nit never performs plate-preparation or plate-processing work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7311`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7311)\n(Precision-instrument Makers and Repairers: `store`/`advisor`/\n`governor`/`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set,\nsame Wave3 rollout, same physical-safety-domain shape) -- cloned and\nread in full in this session. The closed allowlist + always-escalate\nsafety flag + content-based scope-exclusion with a self-trip\nregression test was mirrored closely from that same reference.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7321` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for pre-press technicians,\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Pre-press Technician\nAdvisor ⊣ PrepressTechGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct plate-preparation-execution\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising a plate-preparation-execution\ndecision, or any override of a shop safety officer's judgment. These\nare not merely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- job/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a chemical-exposure/equipment-\n  condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- plate/imaging-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nplate-preparation-execution decision or a shop-safety-officer-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-plate-preparation-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`prepresstech.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-plate-preparation-decision`,\n`:authorize-plate-processing-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-plate-preparation-procedure`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`prepresstech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-plate-preparation-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-plate-processing-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-plate-preparation-procedure`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker record (`:no-worker`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop (`:no-workshop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/shop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   plate-preparation or plate-processing procedure, or overriding a\n   shop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks plate-preparation/plate-processing/safety-\n   override language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a chemical-exposure/\n  equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves the concern\n  itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard data,\"\n  never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  plate/imaging-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  plate-preparation-execution or safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"plate\", \"chemical\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a workshop coordination actor working\nadjacent to plate-preparation/plate-processing work necessarily\ndiscusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could\ntrigger if phrased carelessly.\n`prepresstech.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\nplate-preparation procedure\", \"authorize the plate processing\noperation\", \"override the shop safety officer's judgment\" -- matching\nthe task's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`prepresstech.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nplate-preparation task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`prepresstech.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7321\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7321` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7321`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 47 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-plate-preparation-decision` or\n  `:approve-plate-processing-operation` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to finalize a plate-preparation-execution decision\n  exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For\n  a decision this severe (chemical-exposure hazard from\n  plate-processing), the capability itself must not exist. The only\n  op related to shop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`,\n  which surfaces the need for human/shop-safety-officer attention and\n  never itself decides, authorizes, or defers a plate-preparation\n  decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring earlier\n  reference actors' transaction-amount-ceiling HARD checks): rejected\n  per the task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold\n  plate/imaging-materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is\n  handled as a soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  plate-preparation-execution/safety-officer-override class is a\n  hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"plate\" \"chemical\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  plate/chemical/shop-safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare\n  nouns).\n- Merging `worker` and `workshop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered\n  workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/shop record\n  must be independently verified/registered before any action\" and\n  the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- job/materials-usage/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered worker AND workshop\n   (`:no-worker`/`:no-workshop`). Not a plate-preparation-execution or\n   safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a plate-preparation-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific plate-preparation or plate-processing step -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a chemical-exposure/\n   equipment-condition concern to a human/shop safety officer; ALWAYS\n   escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- plate/imaging-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a\n   plate-preparation-execution or authorization decision of any kind\n   -- it is a purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary\n   cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na plate-preparation-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a\nspecific plate-preparation or plate-processing procedure) or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`prepresstech.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`prepresstech.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`prepresstech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-plate-preparation-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-plate-processing-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-plate-preparation-procedure`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the\n`:op` field (`prepresstech.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a plate-preparation procedure or\noverride a shop safety officer's judgment even via an\notherwise-allowlisted op\n(`prepresstech.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\nThis actor coordinates SHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS ONLY -- it never\nperforms plate-preparation or plate-processing work itself.\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 47, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Pre-press Workshop Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7321"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7321"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7321)), (:test/simulator :prepresstech.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7321 — Pre-press Technicians Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7321)))